55: /**
56:  * A class encapsulating some of the logic around metadata.
57:  * <p>
58:  * This class is shared by the client thread (for partitioning) and the background sender thread.
59:  *
60:  * Metadata is maintained for only a subset of topics, which can be added to over time. When we request metadata for a
61:  * topic we don't have any metadata for it will trigger a metadata update.
62:  * <p>
63:  * If topic expiry is enabled for the metadata, any topic that has not been used within the expiry interval
64:  * is removed from the metadata refresh set after an update. Consumers disable topic expiry since they explicitly
65:  * manage topics while producers rely on topic expiry to limit the refresh set.
66:  */
